Map powerpc64le-unknown-linux-gnu to zig's powerpc64le-linux-gnu.

build.rs hands `cargo`'s TARGET to `zig build -Dtarget=` through a fixed table
and panics on anything not in it ("unsupported target for libghostty-vt
build"), so the whole crate refuses to build on ppc64le before a line of zig
or rust is compiled.  zig and libghostty-vt both support powerpc64le-linux;
only the table was missing the row.

Portability fix worth sending upstream.

--- a/build.rs
+++ b/build.rs
@@ -7,6 +7,7 @@ fn zig_target(target: &str) -> &str {
     match target {
         "x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu" => "x86_64-linux-gnu",
         "aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu" => "aarch64-linux-gnu",
+        "powerpc64le-unknown-linux-gnu" => "powerpc64le-linux-gnu",
         "x86_64-unknown-linux-musl" => "x86_64-linux-musl",
         "aarch64-unknown-linux-musl" => "aarch64-linux-musl",
         "x86_64-apple-darwin" => "x86_64-macos",
